;
A WORD WITH THE SYSOP

A - A word with the sysop

:A
A WORD WITH THE SYSOP

If the sysop is at the local console, you can have a live conversation. From
the CP/M prompt enter:

    CHAT

Leave RBBS with C first if necessary. The program pages the sysop, who answers
at the local console. An unanswered page returns you to CP/M; the sysop may
simply be away from the keyboard.

In the normal display, the sysop types in the upper pane and you type in the
lower one. Each wraps and scrolls independently, so you can type at the same
time without the two conversations becoming intermingled.

Use an 80-column, 24-row ANSI/VT100 terminal. Backspace erases text on the
current line, Tab inserts spaces, and Ctrl-R redraws the display. Ctrl-C or
Ctrl-X ends the conversation.

For simpler terminals, use CHAT /S for the traditional scrolling display.

If nobody answers, don't spend the next ten minutes paging repeatedly. Leave a
note instead:

    MESSAGE

Follow the prompts and save the message. This is a direct submission to the
sysop's review inbox, independent of RBBS mail. An unsaved draft is lost at
call recovery.
